<title>UNITED NATIONS: U.N. panel accepts Iraq oil pricing formula.</title>
<headline>U.N. panel accepts Iraq oil pricing formula.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.N. Security Council sanctions committee on Iraq has accepted the December pricing formula for pending sales of Iraqi crude oil under the U.N. oil-for-food deal, the U.N. announced on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There were no objections to the pricing formula, therefore it was approved,&quot; said U.N. spokesman Ahmad Fawzi.</p>
<p>The United States had blocked adoption of pricing formulas in August and September. American protests were eliminated on Monday after Iraq unconditionally accepted terms of the May 20 accord.</p>
</text>
